            <ArticleTitle>Symptomatic hyponatremia in patients on oxcarbazepine therapy for the treatment of neuropathic pain: two case reports.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>47-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Oxcarbazepine is an FDA approved anticonvulsant medication that has also been used clinically as a treatment for chronic neuropathic pain. Hyponatremia is occasionally seen with the older anticonvulsant carbamazepine, and oxcarbazepine is a derivative of that older drug. Two cases of hyponatremia associated with oxcarbazepine are reported and suggestions for monitoring for and managing this effect are provided.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
